One ClipF variant at a clip_top that is not a multiple of 4.

Against abaire/nxdk_pgraph_tests @ 91a0de45ca31fd03ef2b364347f8a827d226f2b3
("Reenables PVIDEO surface formats that crash xemu. (#316)", 2026-09-18).

This is the whole of #31's missing measurement.  clip_top is read from
kVertSampleCoords, which holds only multiples of 32, so every ClipF capture
that exists has clip_top == 0 (mod 4) -- and on those, 63 different anchoring
rules predict the same anchor.  35 splits them seven ways.  The integer is
chosen, not picked: docs/testing/wbuf_clip_phase_choice.py scores every
candidate, and 34 is strictly weaker than 33 or 35.

It adds one test and changes no existing one: i < 3 reproduces the three
current clip_tops exactly, so WBuf24D_ClipF-150-032/-128/-224 are untouched.
The new test is WBuf24D_ClipF-150-035_V1_ZB0_ZS1.

